text:
doctor_static.py from the livespec plugin cache crashes with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'livespec_runtime'` when invoked from livespec-dev-tooling. The wrapper's _bootstrap.py adds only `scripts/` and `scripts/_vendor/` to sys.path; `livespec_runtime` is a sibling package at /data/projects/livespec-runtime not on the default path.

Workaround: `PYTHONPATH=/data/projects/livespec-runtime:.../scripts ./doctor_static.py`. Surfaced during /livespec:doctor on 2026-05-26; spec findings produced cleanly once the workaround was applied.

Disposition candidates:
(a) doctor_static depends on livespec_runtime.cross_repo.types via depends_on_ref_wellformedness.py — the dep may need vendoring into scripts/_vendor/, or the static check that imports it may need a graceful-skip fallback when the runtime isn't importable;
(b) the livespec plugin's installation may be expected to install livespec_runtime as a peer dep but isn't doing so in this environment;
(c) something env-local to ubuntu's setup that isn't a livespec bug at all.
